      "file": "scenes/scene-2.js",
      "narration": "MP4 plays almost everywhere, so it's the safest bet for uploads. WebM is a solid web format, but sometimes needs converting for a specific destination.",
      "storyboard": "Night stage, wide. A row of device silhouettes: phone, laptop, TV, platform tile. On 'almost everywhere', blue lines from an MP4 chip light every device in sequence. On 'solid web format', a green WebM chip lights three browser icons labeled Chrome, Edge and Firefox. On 'sometimes needs converting', its lines to phone and TV flicker dashed with a small label 'varies', and an LMS tile shows 'check your system'.",
      "minDuration": 10,
      "slide": {
        "title": "MP4 is most portable; WebM suits the web",
        "text": "MP4: phones, computers, TVs, most platforms. WebM: Chrome, Edge and Firefox. WebM on phones and TVs: varies. LMSs: check your system",
        "notes": "MP4 plays almost everywhere, so it's the safest bet for uploads. WebM is a solid web format, but sometimes needs converting for a specific destination.",
